        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cron): llama.cpp rejects unanchored cron tool schema patterns",
        "body": "Fixes #108367\nFixes #108473\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users enabling the `cron` tool would get a hard `400` from llama.cpp-backed providers on every agent message. Providers that convert tool JSON Schema to GBNF reject unanchored `pattern` values with `Pattern must start with '^' and end with '$'`, so the gateway never reaches model inference.\n\nRelated reports: #108367, #108473 (same root cause; #108473 has the fuller repro and captured failure logs).\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nCron schemas advertised a nonblank regex as unanchored `\\S`. llama.cpp's JSON-schema-to-grammar path rejects any `pattern` that is not fully anchored with `^` and `$` ([upstream contract](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/master/grammars/README.md)).\n\nThis PR anchors every affected cron regex while preserving the original **contains at least one non-whitespace character** acceptance set:\n\n- `^[\\s\\S]*\\S[\\s\\S]*$` for `NonBlankString`, `declarationKey`, and `displayName` (addresses ClawSweeper P1: the interim `^\\S(?:.*\\S)?$` form was stricter than the old unanchored `\\S` contract)\n- `^session:.+$` for dynamic session targets\n\nWhitespace-only values still fail; leading/trailing whitespace and multiline display names still pass.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can keep the `cron` tool enabled with llama.cpp-backed OpenAI-compatible providers (Ollama → `llama-server`, Ornith, LM Studio, etc.) without the gateway failing schema conversion before any reply. Existing cron protocol acceptance for normal and boundary-whitespace inputs is preserved.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**ClawSweeper P1 (compatibility semantics) — addressed in `c1b73d6990d`:**\n\n- Pattern updated to `^[\\s\\S]*\\S[\\s\\S]*$` in `packages/gateway-protocol/src/schema/cron.ts` and `src/agents/tools/cron-tool.ts`\n- Regression cases added for `\" daily-report \"`, `\" Daily report \"`, and multiline `displayName` in `src/cron/cron-protocol-schema.test.ts` and `src/agents/tools/cron-tool.schema.test.ts`\n\n**Focused tests (local, post-rebase onto current `main`):**\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/tools/cron-tool.schema.test.ts src/cron/cron-protocol-schema.test.ts test/scripts/prompt-snapshots.test.ts` — 36 passed\n- `node --import tsx scripts/generate-prompt-snapshots.ts --check` — 7 snapshot files current\n- `git diff --check` — clean\n\n**Live llama.cpp behavior proof — pending:**\n\nThis contributor environment has no local `ollama` / `llama-server`, so there is not yet a redacted after-fix agent-turn or gateway log proving inference proceeds with `tools.profile: \"full\"` and `cron` enabled.\n\nValidation path from #108473:\n\n```bash\nopenclaw agent --local --agent main --model ollama/<model> --message \"hi\" --json\n```\n\nIf a maintainer or the original reporter can confirm on head `c22f5db1a6f`, please paste a redacted log snippet in this PR. Schema-level proof matches the reported pre-inference failure mode; live confirmation is the remaining merge gate from ClawSweeper.\n",
        "branch": "fix/cron-schema-anchored-patterns",
